// gl3dgame -- "cube hunter": a real-time, GPU-rendered, interactive 3D game
// in `id`. A camera-relative chase view follows a player cube (WASD moves it
// one grid step at a time); a spinning gold target cube sits somewhere on the
// grid; a field of static gray pillar cubes gives the scene depth. Walking
// the player onto the target's cell scores a point and respawns the target
// elsewhere. Esc/q (or the window close button) quits.
//
//   idc/bin/idc demos/gl3dgame --allow-untested -o gl3dgame && ./gl3dgame
//
// See world/ for the game (world/game) and rendering (world/scene) trees,
// and loop/ for the frame loop. GFX_MAX_FRAMES lets a headless build run N
// frames and exit on its own (see sys/win/gl).

// main()'s no-display path: force_no_display (below) forces glwin_open() to
// fail the same way on every machine, whatever its own DISPLAY is, so ok=0
// and loop(ok) returns through spin's run<=0 branch without ever calling
// frame -- the one path that does not depend on GFX_MAX_FRAMES, an
// environment variable this build does not export.
main(int argc, string[] argv) {
  int ok = glwin_open(800, 600, "id gl3dgame -- cube hunter");
  world_init();
  loop(ok);
} return int 0;
given force_no_display (0, []):(0) then mb_state:("0,0,3,3,0")
given force_no_display (0, []):(0) then calls frame:[0]

// Forces glwin_open() to fail deterministically -- on every machine, whatever
// its own DISPLAY is -- so main()'s no-display path can be cased. idstd's
// env_set (sys/io/ipc/env/write.id) reaches only this one case's own
// process (each case runs in a process of its own).
force_no_display() {
  int r = env_set("DISPLAY", "id-case-no-display");
} return void;
():() then display_probe:(18)
():() then env_error:(0)

// env_get's return is the value's exact byte length, or -1 if the name is
// not set at all -- so this is both "is DISPLAY forced" and "to exactly
// what", in one int. Dropping force_no_display's env_set call turns this
// from 18 into -1, not 0, so it cannot pass by coincidence.
display_probe() {
  int[] buf = [];
  int b = env_get("DISPLAY", buf, 0);
} return int b;
given force_no_display ():(18)
given force_no_display ():(18) then env_error:(0)
